# The plan signing key every build from this repository is expected to use.
#
# This file exists because on 2026-09-23 a tool with a stale path called
# loadOrCreate against a directory the key had been moved out of. It did
# what it was asked: it minted a new key, signed 8,891 runtime install
# scripts with it, and the bases were built with it. Every artifact
# verified perfectly -- against itself. Nothing looked broken. What caught
# it was a second artifact, built at a different moment, disagreeing.
#
# So the expectation is written down here, in the repository, where it is
# reviewable in git and cannot be produced by the same accident that
# produces a key. The tools that make anything we ship check against it
# and refuse: tools/sign_runtime_scripts.mjs, tools/build_site.py,
# src/installers/unix/plankey.sh, src/installers/windows/build.sh, and
# the server at startup.
#
# It is also the thing the Trust page tells a reader to check the
# fingerprint against: "somewhere we do not control" means, for anyone
# who is not us, this file in a public repository.
#
# Changing this line is how the key is rotated. That is a deliberate act
# with a commit attached, which is the whole point. Everything signed by
# the old key stays valid until it is revoked; see docs/operating.md.
#
# The id is the first 16 hex characters of SHA-256 over the raw 32-byte
# Ed25519 public key.
97930ea1888d1a12
